  "worked_solution": "Starting from the equation $u\\cdot v=-2,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $t$ and then solve for $t$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =-2 \\\\ 7\\cdot t+9\\cdot 2+3t\\cdot (-5)+1\\cdot {t}^{2}+(-1)\\cdot 5 & =-2 \\\\ 7t+18-15t+{t}^{2}-5 & =-2 \\\\ {t}^{2}-8t+15 & =0 \\\\ (t-3)(t-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe get two solutions, ${t}_{1}=3$ and ${t}_{2}=5.$ Since we need $t>3$, our final answer is $t=5$ only.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
